    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I tried it and `68.06` → `68.05`, so 0.01kb diff. \r\n\r\n```js\r\n  public unuse(...middlewareToUnuse: Middleware[]): this {\r\n    this.middleware\r\n      .filter(m => middlewareToUnuse.includes(m[0]))\r\n      .forEach(m => m[1].unsubscribe());\r\n\r\n    this.middleware = this.middleware.filter(\r\n      m => !middlewareToUnuse.includes(m[0])\r\n    );\r\n\r\n    return this;\r\n  }\r\n```\r\n\r\nit looks a little bit confusing with [0] and [1].\r\n\r\nWe can use different names for the object instead of `middleware & middlewareDefinition` if you have any idea, like `fn & middleware`?",
    "commit_id": "b0be003dcfee532a136cbb1e97d77aac000476bb",
    "created_at": "2021-03-31T08:18:38Z",
